This package is a Dart port of the behaviour of the official Node.js client
for Brevo, `@getbrevo/brevo` (https://github.com/getbrevo/brevo-node),
version 6.0.3. Request construction, retry policy, error formatting, query and
path encoding and body serialisation follow that implementation, verified by
fixtures captured from it (`test/fixtures/*.json`, produced by
`tool/capture_fixtures/*.js`). No source code of `@getbrevo/brevo` is
reproduced here; that repository ships without a licence file.

Typed models and resource methods are generated from the Brevo OpenAPI
specification published at https://api.brevo.com/v3/swagger_definition_v3.yml,
vendored under `tool/spec/` with its SHA-256 and fetch date recorded in
`tool/spec/SPEC_SHA256` and `tool/spec/SPEC_FETCHED_AT`. Resource and method
names follow the public API surface of `@getbrevo/brevo` so that Brevo's own
documentation applies to this package. The specification declares the MIT
licence (`info.license`, https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT).

The mock-server test tier replays `wiremock/wiremock-mappings.json` from the
official Python client, `brevo-python` (https://github.com/getbrevo/brevo-python),
vendored under `tool/mock/` with its SHA-256 recorded alongside. Those
fixtures are used only to test this package and are not part of what it
ships (`.pubignore` excludes `tool/`). That repository, like `brevo-node`,
carries no licence file; the file is machine-generated request-and-response
metadata derived from the same Brevo specification named above, and
`tool/mock/update_mock.dart` re-downloads it from source on demand.
